    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-01",
      "rank": 1,
      "self_check": {
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "meaning_preserved": true,
        "paragraphs_preserved": true
      },
      "source": "Alice was beginning to get very tired of sitting by her sister on the bank, and of having nothing to do: once or twice she had peeped into the book her sister was reading, but it had no pictures or conversations in it, “and what is the use of a book,” thought Alice “without pictures or conversations?”",
      "terminology_mapping": {
        "Alice": "Alice",
        "bank": "berge",
        "conversations": "dialogues",
        "pictures": "images"
      },
      "translation": "Alice commençait à se lasser fort de rester assise auprès de sa sœur sur la berge, sans rien avoir à faire : une fois ou deux, elle avait jeté un coup d’œil dans le livre que lisait sa sœur, mais il ne contenait ni images ni dialogues. « Et à quoi peut bien servir un livre, songeait Alice, sans images ni dialogues ? »",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-02",
      "rank": 2,
      "self_check": {
        "dialogue_capitalization_emphasis_preserved": true,
        "exact_source": true,
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "meaning_preserved": true,
        "no_additions_or_omissions": true,
        "paragraph_boundaries_preserved": true,
        "style_followed": true
      },
      "source": "So she was considering in her own mind (as well as she could, for the hot day made her feel very sleepy and stupid), whether the pleasure of making a daisy-chain would be worth the trouble of getting up and picking the daisies, when suddenly a White Rabbit with pink eyes ran close by her.",
      "terminology": {
        "White Rabbit": "Lapin Blanc",
        "daisies": "pâquerettes",
        "daisy-chain": "guirlande de pâquerettes"
      },
      "translation": "Elle se demandait donc à part elle (du mieux qu’elle le pouvait, car cette chaude journée lui donnait fort envie de dormir et lui embrouillait l’esprit) si le plaisir de tresser une guirlande de pâquerettes valait la peine de se lever pour aller les cueillir, lorsque soudain un Lapin Blanc aux yeux roses passa en courant tout près d’elle.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-03",
      "rank": 3,
      "self_check": {
        "capitalization_preserved": true,
        "dialogue_preserved": true,
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "literary_register_followed": true,
        "meaning_preserved": true,
        "no_additions_or_omissions": true,
        "paragraph_boundaries_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true
      },
      "source": "There was nothing so very remarkable in that; nor did Alice think it so very much out of the way to hear the Rabbit say to itself, “Oh dear! Oh dear! I shall be late!” (when she thought it over afterwards, it occurred to her that she ought to have wondered at this, but at the time it all seemed quite natural); but when the Rabbit actually took a watch out of its waistcoat-pocket, and looked at it, and then hurried on, Alice started to her feet.",
      "terminology": {
        "Alice": "Alice",
        "Rabbit": "Lapin"
      },
      "translation": "Il n’y avait là rien de bien extraordinaire ; Alice ne trouva pas non plus si étrange d’entendre le Lapin se dire : « Oh là là ! Oh là là ! Je vais être en retard ! » (lorsqu’elle y repensa par la suite, il lui vint à l’esprit qu’elle aurait dû s’en étonner, mais sur le moment tout cela lui avait paru parfaitement naturel) ; mais quand le Lapin tira bel et bien une montre de la poche de son gilet, la consulta, puis repartit en toute hâte, Alice se dressa d’un bond.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-04",
      "rank": 4,
      "self_check": {
        "capitalization_preserved": true,
        "dialogue_preserved": true,
        "emphasis_preserved": true,
        "faithful": true,
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "paragraphs_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true,
        "style_followed": true
      },
      "source": "In another moment down went Alice after it, never once considering how in the world she was to get out again. The rabbit-hole went straight on like a tunnel for some way, and then dipped suddenly down, so suddenly that Alice had not a moment to think about stopping herself before she found herself falling down a very deep well.",
      "terminology": {
        "rabbit-hole": "terrier"
      },
      "translation": "Un instant après, Alice s’y précipita à sa suite, sans se demander une seule fois comment, au monde, elle pourrait bien en ressortir. Le terrier se prolongeait quelque temps tout droit, comme un tunnel, puis plongeait soudain, si brusquement qu’Alice n’eut pas un instant pour songer à se retenir avant de se trouver en train de tomber dans un puits très profond.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-05",
      "rank": 5,
      "self_check": {
        "dialogue_capitalization_emphasis_preserved": true,
        "glossary_and_style_followed": true,
        "paragraph_boundaries_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true,
        "translation_faithful": true
      },
      "source": "Either the well was very deep, or she fell very slowly, for she had plenty of time as she went down to look about her and to wonder what was going to happen next. First, she tried to look down and make out what she was coming to, but it was too dark to see anything; then she looked at the sides of the well, and noticed that they were filled with cupboards and book-shelves; here and there she saw maps and pictures hung upon pegs.",
      "terminology": {
        "book-shelves": "rayonnages",
        "cupboards": "placards",
        "pegs": "chevilles",
        "well": "puits"
      },
      "translation": "Ou bien le puits était très profond, ou bien elle tombait très lentement, car elle eut tout le temps, au cours de sa descente, de regarder autour d’elle et de se demander ce qui allait arriver ensuite. D’abord, elle essaya de regarder en bas et de distinguer où elle allait aboutir, mais il faisait trop sombre pour voir quoi que ce fût ; puis elle regarda les parois du puits et remarqua qu’elles étaient garnies de placards et de rayonnages ; çà et là, elle vit des cartes et des images suspendues à des chevilles.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-06",
      "rank": 6,
      "self_check": {
        "dialogue_capitalization_emphasis_preserved": true,
        "faithful": true,
        "glossary_compliant": true,
        "idiomatic_literary_french": true,
        "paragraph_boundaries_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true
      },
      "source": "She took down a jar from one of the shelves as she passed; it was labelled “ORANGE MARMALADE,” but to her great disappointment it was empty: she did not like to drop the jar for fear of killing somebody underneath, so managed to put it into one of the cupboards as she fell past it.",
      "terminology": {
        "ORANGE MARMALADE": "MARMELADE D’ORANGES"
      },
      "translation": "Au passage, elle prit sur l’une des étagères un pot portant l’étiquette « MARMELADE D’ORANGES », mais, à son grand désappointement, il était vide : comme elle ne voulait pas laisser tomber le pot, de peur de tuer quelqu’un au-dessous, elle parvint à le déposer dans l’un des placards devant lesquels elle passait au cours de sa chute.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-07",
      "rank": 7,
      "self_check": {
        "capitalization_preserved": true,
        "dialogue_preserved": true,
        "emphasis_markers_preserved": true,
        "faithful": true,
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "paragraphs_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true,
        "style_followed": true
      },
      "source": "“Well!” thought Alice to herself, “after such a fall as this, I shall think nothing of tumbling down stairs! How brave they’ll all think me at home! Why, I wouldn’t say anything about it, even if I fell off the top of the house!” (Which was very likely true.)",
      "terminology": {
        "Alice": "Alice"
      },
      "translation": "« Eh bien ! songea Alice, après une chute pareille, je ne ferai plus aucun cas de dégringoler dans l’escalier ! Comme ils vont tous me trouver courageuse, à la maison ! Ma foi, je n’en dirais rien, quand bien même je tomberais du haut de la maison ! » (Ce qui était très probablement vrai.)",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "alice-08",
      "rank": 8,
      "self_check": {
        "capitalization_preserved": true,
        "dialogue_preserved": true,
        "emphasis_markers_preserved": true,
        "glossary_followed": true,
        "idiomatic_literary_french": true,
        "meaning_preserved": true,
        "no_additions_or_omissions": true,
        "paragraph_boundaries_preserved": true,
        "source_exact": true
      },
      "source": "Down, down, down. Would the fall never come to an end? “I wonder how many miles I’ve fallen by this time?” she said aloud. “I must be getting somewhere near the centre of the earth. Let me see: that would be four thousand miles down, I think—” (for, you see, Alice had learnt several things of this sort in her lessons in the schoolroom, and though this was not a very good opportunity for showing off her knowledge, as there was no one to listen to her, still it was good practice to say it over).",
      "terminology": {
        "Alice": "Alice"
      },
      "translation": "Elle descendait, descendait, descendait. Cette chute ne finirait-elle donc jamais ? « Je me demande combien de milles j’ai bien pu tomber jusqu’à présent », dit-elle tout haut. « Je dois approcher quelque part du centre de la Terre. Voyons : cela ferait quatre mille milles de profondeur, je crois— » (car, voyez-vous, Alice avait appris plusieurs choses de ce genre pendant ses leçons, dans la salle de classe ; et bien que l’occasion fût assez mal choisie pour faire étalage de son savoir, puisqu’il n’y avait personne pour l’écouter, c’était tout de même un bon exercice que de le répéter).",
      "uncertainties": []
    }
  ],
